invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/hash-builds.sh
reason: sha512_hw.c drops the target attribute that turns the SHA-512
  instructions on for its own functions, so the file compiles only where
  the whole object is built with the instruction flag, and an object
  built that way may run them in code no CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512 bit
  ever chose. The script compiles the file for arm64 with no instruction
  flag and requires the five entries and the instructions there.

--- old
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((target("sha3"))), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#pragma GCC target("+sha3")
#endif
--- new
#ifdef __clang__
#pragma clang attribute push(__attribute__((cold)), apply_to = function)
#else
#pragma GCC push_options
#endif
